{
  "name": "@takk/bayesroute",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "BayesRoute: Thompson-sampling Bayesian router that picks the right LLM for every query across quality, cost, and latency for Massive Intelligence (IM) products and agents. A zero-runtime-dependency, TypeScript-first library that keeps an exact conjugate posterior per (model, domain) arm, a Beta over acceptable-output probability for quality and a Gamma-Exponential model over response time and token cost, then samples each posterior and routes to the arm with the highest expected utility, so model selection is a calibrated probabilistic decision that explores and exploits with bounded regret, not a static rule or a greedy top-model heuristic. Closed-form online updates with zero inference latency, explicit per-domain priors, safe-exploration bounds that cap regression risk, optional time-decay for stale evidence and silent model deprecations, a tamper-evident hash-chained audit trail for compliance, and a node-free core that runs in Node, edge runtimes, and the browser, with optional peers @takk/bayestruth, @takk/keymesh, @takk/modelchain, @takk/behavioralai, @takk/noeticos, @takk/racs, @takk/gaptime, @takk/krikos, @takk/mcpcustoms, @takk/alkaline, @takk/tokenforecast, @takk/agenticstash and @takk/automend.",
